3.6 **Reporting.** ATS shall provide LPA with:
(a) A monthly operational report, including cargo volumes, vessel calls, and equipment availability, within fifteen (15) days after the end of each month;
(b) A quarterly performance report against the targets in Clause 3.5, within thirty (30) days after the end of each quarter; and
(c) An annual business plan and capital expenditure forecast, for the following Year, at least ninety (90) days before the start of that Year.

3.7 **Regulatory Compliance.** ATS shall obtain and maintain all permits, licences, and approvals required for its operations, including those from NPA, NIMASA, and the Federal Ministry of Transport. ATS shall promptly notify LPA of any material breach or threatened breach of any regulatory requirement.

3.8 **Environmental Obligations.** ATS shall conduct its operations in accordance with the Environmental Management Plan set out in Schedule D, and shall:
(a) Manage waste, including ship-generated waste and cargo residues, in accordance with applicable regulations;
(b) Minimise emissions and noise, having regard to best available techniques; and
(c) Cooperate with LPA and regulatory authorities in the event of any environmental incident, including spills or releases.

3.9 **Health and Safety.** ATS shall:
(a) Maintain a health and safety management system consistent with international standards;
(b) Provide appropriate personal protective equipment to all personnel and visitors;
(c) Conduct regular safety drills, including fire and emergency response exercises, at least once per quarter;
(d) Report all accidents, incidents, and near misses to LPA within twenty-four (24) hours; and
(e) Cooperate with any safety audit or inspection conducted by LPA or its agents.

3.10 **Liaison with LPA.** ATS shall meet with LPA representatives at least monthly to review operational performance, discuss issues, and coordinate activities. ATS shall also provide a designated liaison officer who shall be available during normal working hours to respond to LPA enquiries.

