**ARTICLE 4: MAINTENANCE AND REPAIR**

4.1 **Standard of Maintenance.** ATS shall maintain the Concession Assets in good repair and operating condition, ordinary wear and tear excepted, so as to ensure the safe and efficient operation of the Terminal.

4.2 **Routine Maintenance.** ATS shall carry out routine maintenance in accordance with the manufacturers’ recommendations and good industry practice, including:
(a) Daily inspections of quay cranes, yard equipment, and reefer points;
(b) Scheduled servicing of all mechanical and electrical equipment;
(c) Regular cleaning and upkeep of pavements, drainage, and markings; and
(d) Prompt repair of any damage caused by normal operations.

4.3 **Major Maintenance and Replacement.** ATS shall prepare and submit to LPA for approval a five-year maintenance and capital replacement plan, to be updated annually. The plan shall identify the anticipated timing and cost of major repairs and replacements, including the replacement of major equipment at the end of its useful life.

4.4 **Emergency Repairs.** In the event of any breakdown or damage that affects or threatens to affect operations, ATS shall:
(a) Take immediate steps to make the affected asset safe and, where practicable, to restore service;
(b) Notify LPA as soon as reasonably practicable, and in any event within six (6) hours;
(c) Carry out emergency repairs at its own cost, except where the damage is caused by LPA’s negligence or a force majeure event; and
(d) Provide LPA with a written report of the incident within seven (7) days.
